The original query related to a kernel panic seemingly caused by the NFS
v3 server code in a cluster running Tru64 v5.1B with all current patches.  
This problem brought the entire cluster down repeatedly and was difficult 
to trace as a result. The clients are Linux boxes (2.2 & 2.4 kernels).

It transpires that the crash is caused by a problem in the AdvFS code
which can be indirectly persuaded to write out-of-bounds by an NFS client.  
>From the initial support query on 27th May, HP have just furnished me with
a patch and this should be included in a future patch kit release.

--
John P.



