Hi,

On Mon, 23 Jun 2003 14:32:43 I wrote:

>We have a TZ89 on an XP 1000, Tru64 UNIX V4.0G. The drive is used
>exclusively for nightly backups with dump. The equipment is some
>3 years old and has functioned perfectly until now.
>
>During the last few weeks the drive has gone offline twice for no
>obvious reason. I.e., scu show edt does not list it. Trying to
>access the drive by mt or file hangs for a while, then there is a
>message saying no such device. There are also corresponding entries
>in the error log. The device does however come back if we reboot the
>machine.
>
>Has anyone on this list seen similar behaviour, and if so, how did
>you solve the problem? I would appreciate any help or direction.
>

I got very helpful replies from Richard Mollel, Martin Rønde Andersen
and Alan Rollow. I learnt that I could try to get the drive back
on-line by first power cycling it and then scan the bus with
scu scan edt
This worked. The reason for the failure is not clear yet, however.
I have exchanged the SCSI cable, but since there was another failure
after this the cable is probably not be the reason. I believe more
in Martin's idea that I got some bad tapes. Time will show, I hope.

Thanks for the helpful suggestions,

Bjorn 
