Numerous people pointed me to the mount man page; thanks to all.

The 'man 8 mount' page contains the following mount options which
determines the behavior:
  
grpid
    Enables new files to inherit the parent directory's group ID.
    This is the default and matches BSD semantics.
  
nogrpid
    Applies SVID 3 semantics.    For example, if the parent
    directory's mode bits include IS_GID, then the new file
    will inherit the parent's group ID.  If IS_GID is off,
    then it inherits the process group ID.
  

