Hi All,

The answer to my question (see below) is, to re-configure the
swapping from EAGER to LAZY in the /etc/sysconftab file.  By
default, T64 will set this to EAGER, meaning it will allocate
(reserve) memory for each process.  By resetting this to LAZY
mode, memory will only be allocated when needed.

If one has less swap space than physical memory (which is what
I have), best thing to do is set this to LAZY.

Thanks for all who replied!! My system is working great now!

(now, off to hunt down a newer copy of the CXX compiler, since=20
my V6.3 is kinda old and rusty..)

Cheers,
	Fred

